1. HARDWARE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CPU      MC68HC11F1, big-endian. RAM 0000-03FF internal + 1810-1FFF external. EEPROM 0E00 (seed/key).
Flash    28F010 128K, address lines A1/A13, A2/A12, A3/A11, A10/A14 swapped on the chip.
Map      bank0 $2000-$FFFF (cal $2000-$58FF, common code $5900-$7FFF, bank-0 code $8000+)
         bank1 $8000-$FFFF, selected by PORTG bit 3. Common code calls bank 1 through the
         far-call wrappers at 7C23-7E3F (ldx #$1002 / bset 0,x,#$08 / jsr / bclr).
Chips    IOR 66285 at $1800 (outputs, switch inputs, 4 PWM pairs), TIO 39985 at $1400-$16FF
         (pump encoder, CKP, injection counters, PCS current), J1850 controller at $0C02/$0C03.
Checksum 16-bit sum of bank0 $2006-$FFFF + bank1 $8000-$FFFF, stored at $2004.

IOR $1800 outputs            .0 glow relay  .1 ITS (timing stepper) enable  .2 Service Throttle lamp
                             .3 EGR vent  .4/.5 shift solenoids A/B  .6 glow wait-lamp (see note)
                             .7 PCS low drive
IOR $1802                    .7-.4 AMUX select, .3 4WD, .2 perf shift sw, .1 manual shift sw, .0 cruise on/off
IOR $1804 inputs             .7 resume/accel .6 set/coast .5/.4/.3 range pressure sw B/C/A .2 TCC brake
                             .1 brake .0 PTO
IOR $1807                    .3 MIL .2 pump trim resistor read .1 trans temp pullup .0 IAT pullup
IOR PWM pairs (freq, duty)   1808/1809 TCC PWM solenoid (4L80E)   180A/180B boost (wastegate)
                             180C/180D 4L60E 3-2 solenoid channel - not used   180E/180F EGR
Timer    TIC1 VSS, TIC2 trans input shaft, TIC3 8X pump cam, TIC4 4X crank, TOC3 160 Hz scheduler,
         TOC4 backup injection pulse, TOC1 backup fuel, TOC2 NOT USED. PD5 power-down.
ADC      AN0/1/3 pedal APP1-3, AN2 force-motor current, AN4 battery, AN5 boost, AN6 AMUX, AN7 EGR/baro.
AMUX     MUX0 glow V, 1 fuel temp, 2 diag sw, 3 ECT, 4 spare, 5 pump cal, 6 QDM1 fault, 7 glow
         relay supply, 8 QDM2 fault, 9 A/C request, 10 IAT, 11 optical 5V, 13 trans temp,
         14 APP2 5V, 15 flash Vpp. Results in RAM 1941-1950.

Corrections to the 1000cows notes (its OBD2 list is the OBD1 list with $14xx -> $18xx):
  - TOC2 is not the TCC PWM on OBD2. OBD1 made the TCC PWM in software on TOC2/PA6; OBD2 uses the
    IOR PWM 1808/1809 and never touches TOC2 (vector = rti, TCTL1 = 0).
  - 1808/1809 is not "PCS current": 1809 goes to 0 on brake and when the TCC command is 0. The PCS
    force-motor current is commanded through TIO $1400.
  - 1800.6 is driven only by the glow code (with the glow relay, plus a glow timer) = wait lamp.
    On the OBD1 board it was the 4L60E TCC on/off solenoid.


