3. HOW THE OS RUNS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reset 5900 area: init HC11 (cal table 50B6), IOR (cal table 5099), TIO (b1:8000 data), RAM.
Background loop Main_task_scheduler 5B5C; 160 Hz TOC3 tick -> 12.5/25/50 ms jobs (OBD1 names
_run_12ms_job, _run_25ms_job 80CF, _run_50ms_job 8D76).
Table lookups: lookup_2D_table 6D06 (X=table [N][N+1 pts], A=input), lookup_3D_table 6D20
(X=table, A=column, B=row, header cols=(h&F)+2 rows=(h>>4)+2), 17-point no-header 66E5,
offset tables 66C8/6702, curve 67D3.
Scaling: RPM byte N*18.75 (engine_RPM 1986 is 16-bit), VSS mph N*0.5, fuel mm3 N*0.3125,
battery N/10 V, boost kPa N, baro N*0.5, timing deg N*0.1, pedal % N/2.56, gear = N+1.
Option bytes: 200B (.1 turbo .2 TCM/no internal trans .3 low-res limp .7 PTO ...),
200C (.0 delta-fuel limiter .4 trans torque reduction .5/.6 baro source), 200D (.3 trans
sensors on ECM ...). Full legend at the top of the cal in the NOTED file.


4. FUEL / PUMP / TIMING (from the code + 1000cows)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Stanadyne DS4 with optical encoder (64/cyl + 1/cyl). Pump reference = 22.2 crank deg before SOI.
Fuel = crank degrees from pump reference to end of injection: READ_PUMP_MAPS (b1:963B) adds the
low/high-fuel 3D pump map and the 2D table, then pump-resistor trim (Pump_Cal_Ptr from the table at
b1:81D1). Fuel tables clip at fuel_quantity $133 (96 mm3) but fuel_quantity is a byte (79.7 mm3 max).
Timing: desired = base + ECT + baro + IAT adders; ITS stepper drives measured timing to it.
Limits: over-rev cut $E7 = 4331 rpm (150 rpm hysteresis), safety limiter 203B-203E, governor 2271-2287.
Backup mode (no hi-res signal): TOC4 backup pulses from the 8X cam / 4X crank, heavily derated.


5. TRANSMISSION (4L80E as built)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Outputs: shift A/B 1800.4/.5, TCC PWM 1809, PCS force motor via TIO $1400 (current loop,
FORCE_MTR_ITERM). Inputs: VSS TIC1, input shaft TIC2, range switches 1804.3-.5, trans temp MUX13.
Speeds: calc_input_shaft_speed_raw 9612, CALC_OSS_SPEED 96C4, shared period math 96F9,
"throttle" for shift/TCC tables calc_tp_for_transmission 9746 (pedal or cruise fuel).
Shift schedule: calc_shift_request_E4B2 uses pointer sets E3B4 (up) / E3C0 (down) / E3CC (RPM):
[pattern bit mask][stride] records pointing at 17-point cal curves 3920-3B0B.
TCC apply/release: records D4F7-D596, release logic E20A, slip PI DFEA.
All 44 cals are 4L80E with input speed sensor (3864 = $80); "TCM" cals ($A0) hand the trans to an
external controller.

4L60E: no OS on file (OBD1 BPDP + 16 OBD2 families) has 3-2 or TCC-on/off control logic.
  - 3-2 channel = IOR PWM 180C/180D. OBD1 set its freq to $7A (~50 Hz if the register is a
    divider: $BF ~32 Hz EGR/boost, $09 force motor). OBD2 sets it to 0 ($50B2 freq, $50B4 duty).
  - Bench test without code: $50B2 = $7A, $50B4 = $80 -> fixed 50% from key-on; probe the unused
    C1/C3 pins. If nothing toggles, the driver is not fitted on the OBD2 board.
  - Writing it: 3-2 duty table in cal, routine in the 50 ms trans job using shift_event_flags $77,
    trans_gear_AT, VEHICLE_SPEED_0, engine_load_est_filtered. Free code: 7F14-7FFF (236 bytes, common)
    or b1:FE8C-FFBE (307 bytes). A full 4L60E swap also needs range-switch decode (code at 9606),
    shift solenoid pattern, TCC on/off, PCS curves and the no-input-speed mode (3864 bit 7 clear).


